{
  "manufacturer": "Lochinvar",
  "manufacturer_slug": "lochinvar",
  "model": "Crest",
  "model_slug": "crest",
  "aliases": [
    "Crest FB",
    "Crest OF",
    "Crest FCB",
    "Hellcat"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Condensing boiler controller",
  "applies_to": "Crest FB/OF 751-6001 and FCB 1000-6000 condensing boilers (the manual uses the same map for Hellcat).",
  "summary": "The Crest boiler exposes BACnet MS/TP through Lochinvar's Modbus/BACnet communication board. Besides the usual enable, temperature, firing rate and status/blocking/lockout codes, larger and FCB models add dual-burner, damper, O2 trim and cascade member lockout points.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": "Base + MAC address: 610000 for FB 751-2001, 670000 for FB 2501-6001, 680000 for FCB1000-6000 (base can be changed)",
  "notes": [
    "BACnet needs the optional Lochinvar Modbus/BACnet communication board; address and baud rate are set on its dip switches.",
    "The BACnet board is an MS/TP master only, so MAC addresses 0-127 are usable.",
    "AV 0 (Configuration) is a bitmask: set a bit to 1 to make the appliance use the BAS-written value instead of its own input.",
    "BAS-supplied temperatures must be rewritten every few seconds and other commands at least every 4 minutes, or the unit reverts to local control.",
    "Temperatures are in °C on the bus.",
    "Several points only exist on certain Crest sizes; the size range is given in the point description."
  ],
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Pick the BMS control mode at the boiler, then write AV 0 Configuration so the unit knows which values the BAS will supply. After that the BAS sends an enable, a rate command (AV 2), or both, and keeps rewriting them. Status, temperatures and the status, blocking and lockout codes can be read without taking control.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "AV 0",
        "name": "Configuration",
        "why": "Tells the unit which inputs come from the BAS; resend before commands"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 0",
        "name": "Boiler Enable",
        "why": "Enable / call for heat from the BAS"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 2",
        "name": "0-10 Volt Input / Rate Command / Setpoint Command",
        "why": "Rate command: firing % or setpoint, per BMS Type"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 8",
        "name": "Outlet Temperature",
        "why": "Outlet temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 11",
        "name": "Firing Rate",
        "why": "Firing rate"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 13",
        "name": "Boiler Status Code",
        "why": "Status code"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 15",
        "name": "Boiler Lockout Code",
        "why": "Lockout code"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 5",
        "name": "Outdoor Temperature",
        "why": "Outdoor temperature from the BAS, if used"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "Set the Demand Configuration under Main Menu > Setup > BMS. ENABLE active / BMS inactive: local setpoints plus BV 0 enable. ENABLE and BMS active: BV 0 enable plus AV 2 rate or setpoint command. ENABLE inactive / BMS active: AV 2 modulation % or setpoint alone. Always set the matching AV 0 bits first. AV 2 means firing % or temperature setpoint depending on the BMS Type setting (Power or Setpoint); as a setpoint it is scaled like a 0-10 V signal between the BMS temperatures at low and high input.",
    "heartbeat": "If BAS-written temperatures stop arriving within the timeout, the unit reverts to its own sensor inputs. On Crest the timeout is programmable from 5 to 120 s (Main Menu > Setup > BAS); Lochinvar recommends the shortest value. On Hellcat and Regent it is fixed at 300 s. Other commands must be refreshed at least every 4 minutes or the boiler runs on its own inputs.",
    "remote_sensors": "Set the AV 0 bits for the values the BAS will supply, then write them to the analog values: AV 3 tank setpoint, AV 4 tank temperature, AV 5 outdoor temperature, AV 6 system supply temperature, AV 7 system return temperature. Values are in °C. Temperatures must be rewritten every few seconds or the unit returns to its own sensors.",
    "setup": [
      "MAC address from dip switches 1-8 (master only, so 0-127); baud from switches 9-10: 9600, 19200, 38400 or 76800.",
      "Device instance = base + MAC address; bases are 610000 (FB 751-2001), 670000 (FB 2501-6001) and 680000 (FCB1000-6000). The base can be changed (0-4194048)."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "The manual says to resend the AV 0 configuration bits before each command.",
      "In a cascade only the Leader needs the BACnet board for control; it then reports cascade totals only, so fit a board to every unit to see each one.",
      "Without BMS mode active the board is monitor-only: the read-only points can be polled while the unit runs on its own controls.",
      "Several BI/AI points exist only on certain Crest sizes or on FCB models; check the size notes in each description."
    ]
  },
  "source": {
    "title": "Modbus and BACnet Communication Instructions (Crest FB/OF751-6001, FCB1000-6000 & Regent IWH500-1000)",
    "doc_number": "100161012_2000020084",
